cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "Diff-IrisPAD: Unsupervised Iris Presentation Attack Detection via Latent Brownian Bridge Diffusion Models"
authors:
  - family-names: "Yadav"
    given-names: "Harsh"
  - name: "Group 18, IIT Mandi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/[TO-BE-ADDED]"
institution:
  name: "Indian Institute of Technology Mandi"
  department: "School of Computing and Electrical Engineering"
course: "CS671 Deep Learning, Spring 2026"
abstract: >
  Diff-IrisPAD is an unsupervised iris presentation attack detection system
  that trains a Latent Brownian Bridge Diffusion Model (LBBDM-f4) on bona fide
  iris images only and detects attacks via ViT-B/16 cosine reconstruction
  divergence. Achieves ACER 0.276 on LivDet-Iris 2025 across 8 attack types,
  outperforming supervised baselines including DINOv2.
keywords:
  - iris presentation attack detection
  - diffusion models
  - Brownian bridge
  - unsupervised anomaly detection
  - biometrics
license: MIT
year: 2026
